    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic coronary disease with stable angina (I25.119)</content>. No angina on medical therapy and cardiac rehabilitation; blood pressure 124/76, at goal. LDL 51 mg/dL on atorvastatin and ezetimibe, at the goal of below 55 mg/dL; total cholesterol 118, HDL 44, triglycerides 115 mg/dL. Weight down 2.4 kg. [S]<list><item>Continue aspirin, atorvastatin 80 mg, ezetimibe 10 mg and metoprolol succinate 25 mg.</item><item>Finish the 36 rehabilitation sessions, then a home exercise plan.</item><item>Lipid panel in 6 to 12 months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute low back strain (S39.012A)</content>. Resolved. [S]<list><item>Lift with the legs; ask a player to help with heavy bags.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Squamous cell carcinoma of the left lower lip, excised (C00.1)</content>. No sign of recurrence about twelve weeks after excision. [S]<list><item>Next lip, mouth and neck examination in about five weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Examination of the lips, mouth, and neck</td><td>Every 1 to 3 months in year 1, 2 to 6 months in year 2, 4 to 8 months in years 3 to 5, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No recurrence or new lesion; no neck nodes</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sun protection of the lips and skin</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Lip balm with sunscreen and a hat daily</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco and alcohol use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tobacco-free</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Dental evaluation</td><td>After diagnosis, then routine</td><td>Due</td><td>Not yet arranged; he is deciding where to go</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure (goal below 130/80)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>124/76, at goal</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI, and physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>91.6 kg, BMI 26.8; rehabilitation three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Angina frequency and nitroglycerin use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None; no nitroglycerin</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and side effects: aspirin, high-intensity statin, beta-blocker</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>All taken daily, with ezetimibe; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>4 to 12 weeks after starting or changing lipid therapy, then every 3 to 12 months; goal LDL below 55 mg/dL</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ten weeks after adding ezetimibe: total cholesterol 118, LDL 51, HDL 44, triglycerides 115 mg/dL; at goal</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Cardiac rehabilitation</td><td>After a heart attack or for stable angina: up to 36 sessions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>18 of 36 sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2 or PHQ-9)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-2 1 at intake; next at the preventive visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Lip cancer removed with clear margins and no recurrence on surveillance through four months. In progress; target 1951-10-26 [S]</item><item>LDL cholesterol below 55 mg/dL on secondary prevention. Outcome by 1951-09-21: LDL 51 mg/dL on atorvastatin 80 mg and ezetimibe 10 mg [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg. Outcome by 1951-09-21: 124/76 on metoprolol [S]</item><item>Complete cardiac rehabilitation and walk uphill without angina. In progress; target 1951-10-26 [S]</item><item>Stay tobacco-free and protect his lips and skin from the sun. In progress; target 1951-10-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Head and Neck Cancers (cancer of the lip and oral cavity) (2026); 2023 AHA/ACC/ACCP/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline for the Management of Patients With Chronic Coronary Disease (2023); 2018 AHA/ACC/AACVPR/AAPA/ABC/ACPM/ADA/AGS/APhA/ASPC/NLA/PCNA Guideline on the Management of Blood Cholesterol (2018); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, ischemic heart disease monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit in two weeks. Lip surveillance and coronary disease review in about five weeks. Next scheduled visit 1951-10-05: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

